WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:14,660
Hello, this is Ann, certified nutritionist and genetic specialist with Connors Clinic.

00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:17,620
And today we're going to be talking about acetylcholine.

00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:23,740
So what is acetylcholine and why is it important?

00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:28,300
Acetylcholine is the most plentiful neurotransmitter in the human body.

00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:33,100
It's the neurotransmitter that sends signals to our muscles so they can activate and move

00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,100
our bodies.

00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:39,500
And it's also a neurotransmitter that is essential for brain health because of its involvement

00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,100
in thought, learning, and memory.

00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:48,620
It's so important for our brains that the deficit of acetylcholine is linked to Alzheimer's

00:00:48,620 --> 00:00:49,620
disease.

00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:57,060
It's the neurotransmitter that actually tells the hippocampus to store a memory.

00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:03,940
Acetylcholine is made in our neurons and the nutrient colon is required for its production.

00:01:03,940 --> 00:01:09,980
You can get colon in the foods that you eat like eggs and meat and your body can also

00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:13,540
make colon by way of the PEMT gene.

00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:17,940
And there's two things that influence the PEMT gene.

00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:25,980
First is estrogen, the hormone estrogen, and the second is variance in the PEMT gene.

00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:33,460
So estrogen is what's going to turn on the PEMT gene and then variance in the PEMT make

00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:38,300
it so that the gene is not working to its full potential.

00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:45,700
So if you have low estrogen and or variance in the PEMT gene, then your body is not producing

00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:53,500
enough colon, which then obviously can lead to low acetylcholine production.

00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:59,100
I think it's also important to note that there are studies that show that high intake of

00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:05,860
colon by pregnant women results in higher cognitive performance of the developing child for

00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:09,020
his, his or her entire life.

00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:14,740
And it really can reduce the risk of that child ever developing dementia later in life.

00:02:14,740 --> 00:02:22,020
So it's super important for pregnant women to take colon for obviously brain health for

00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:24,260
their developing babies.

00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:28,860
And it's also really important for vegans to supplement with colon since the foods that

00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:35,810
are highest sources of colon tend to be animal products.

00:02:35,810 --> 00:02:39,770
These are some of the supplements that we offer here at Conor's Clinic that will support

00:02:39,770 --> 00:02:43,410
your production of colon and acetylcholine.

